The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
vi->rss_hdr = devm_kzalloc(&dev->dev, virtnet_rss_hdr_size(vi), GFP_KERNEL);
devm_kfree(&dev->dev, vi->rss_hdr);
devm_kfree(&dev->dev, old_rss_hdr);
```
Reason:  
The initial rss_hdr allocation (in `virtnet_probe`) uses `vi->vdev->dev` (virtio_device), but in `virtnet_set_queues()` all devm operations incorrectly pass `&dev->dev` (net_device). devm resources must be freed with the same device pointer used for allocation; the mismatch triggers a kernel resource tracking warning.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
vi->rss_hdr = devm_kzalloc(&vi->vdev->dev, virtnet_rss_hdr_size(vi), GFP_KERNEL);
devm_kfree(&vi->vdev->dev, vi->rss_hdr);
devm_kfree(&vi->vdev->dev, old_rss_hdr);
```
Reason:  
Using `&vi->vdev->dev` (virtio_device) consistently for both allocation and deallocation ensures the devres API sees the same owner device, eliminating the warning and preventing resource tracking errors.

